"name":"B. Wickens, Jennifer","rank":114,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"46","corresponding":null,"first":"Victoria","key":"bwickensvictoriapau","last":"B. Wickens","name":"B. Wickens, Victoria","rank":115,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"winsamariepau","last":"Winsa","name":"Winsa, Marie","rank":116,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 56","corresponding":null,"first":"Leana","key":"zollerleanapau","last":"Zoller","name":"Zoller, Leana","rank":117,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ignasi","key":"bartomeusignasipau","last":"Bartomeus","name":"Bartomeus, Ignasi","rank":118,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/geb.70000","issn":["1466822X","14668238"],"issn_org":["1466822X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Global Ecology and Biogeography","paperid":"e70000","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Global Ecology and Biogeography","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216592677"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-88fde199-d143-439b-9380-4712baf2d208"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"EuPPollNet: A European Database of Plant-Pollinator Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-796572","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The mental and emotional burden of living with a chronic disease, such as Rheumatoid Arthritis (RA), calls for a better understanding of how we can support people in coping through affectively designed healthcare technologies. This paper presents findings from an ongoing research project concerned with redesigning an existing self-tracking app towards better supporting affective dimensions of living with RA. On the basis of an exploratory, intervention-based design study, we present three overall affective needs feeding into three design opportunities for cultivating affective and emotional dimensions in the redesign of the app; 1) creating a digital room for emotional response, 2) offering a space for mindfulness and 3) helping people to own their RA story. Our results emphasize the need for HCI and design researchers to approach the design of healthcare technology holistically, which includes exploring affective interactions that empower people to develop more sustainable coping strategies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kühn, Lena","Boer, Laurens","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798563"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Health","Mental wellbeing","Rheumatoid arthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring app based affective interactions for people with rheumatoid arthritis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.895","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798563","ids":["itu-ded5b5ed-01c7-4c36-a207-212a1efc1f7b"],"keyword":["affective interaction design","affective interactions","health","mental wellbeing","rheumatoid arthritis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-55B7F02765B6352A391DBACCA8CCE820"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.895","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"kühnpau","last":"Kühn","name":"Kühn, Lena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2024.895","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of DRS2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ded5b5ed-01c7-4c36-a207-212a1efc1f7b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring app-based affective interactions for people with rheumatoid arthritis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798563","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper reports on our ongoing research focusing on cultivating and exploring the topic of what we refer to as breathing commons. We approach breathing as an affective and somatic bodily function that ties the individual with the collective, and through that aim to foster affective commoning among bodies. We present two workshops, one physical and one online, that we have ran amongst our research group on breathing commons. Three themes emerged from the analysis of the workshop activities: a) The body as a membrane, b) feelings of intimacy, vulnerability and awkwardness, and c) mutual engagement and care. These show a path towards engaging with breathing, and potentially with other bodily functions and biodata, aiming to open up the design space of doing affective commoning through bodily functions that act as a connection between bodies – both human and non-human.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Kühn, Lena","Ryding, Karin","Hartmann, Mai","Fritsch, Jonas","Foverskov, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382594"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Affective Commoning","Breathing Commons","Collective Intimacy","Design Space Biodata","Somatic Bodily Function"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"breathing commons affective and somatic relations between self and others","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86283295/BREATHING_COMMONS_AFFECTIVE_AND_SOMATIC_RELATIONS_BETWEEN_SELF_AND_OTHERS_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382594","ids":["itu-595a8ea9-4a43-4e61-8281-413de86655f4"],"keyword":["Affective Commoning","Breathing Commons","Collective Intimacy","Design Space Biodata","Somatic Bodily Function"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-53B577E599AB9DC688F3018C6D5B5D8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86283295/BREATHING_COMMONS_AFFECTIVE_AND_SOMATIC_RELATIONS_BETWEEN_SELF_AND_OTHERS_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Vasiliki-Tsaknaki/publication/353945970_BREATHING_COMMONS_AFFECTIVE_AND_SOMATIC_RELATIONS_BETWEEN_SELF_AND_OTHERS/links/611b70df1e95fe241ad87458/BREATHING-COMMONS-AFFECTIVE-AND-SOMATIC-RELATIONS-BETWEEN-SELF-AND-OTHERS.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"kühnpau","last":"Kühn","name":"Kühn, Lena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"rydingpau","last":"Ryding","name":"Ryding, Karin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mai","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"c4e4fa45-a84f-4422-a4f5-7cc5706782a2","name":"Hartmann, Mai","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Maria","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-595a8ea9-4a43-4e61-8281-413de86655f4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"BREATHING COMMONS: AFFECTIVE AND SOMATIC RELATIONS BETWEEN SELF AND OTHERS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382594","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Scientific data analyses often combine several computational tools in automated pipelines, or workflows. Thousands of such workflows have been used in the life sciences, though their composition has remained a cumbersome manual process due to a lack of standards for annotation, assembly, and implementation. Recent technological advances have returned the long-standing vision of automated workflow composition into focus. This article summarizes a recent Lorentz Center workshop dedicated to automated composition of workflows in the life sciences. We survey previous initiatives to automate the composition process, and discuss the current state of the art and future perspectives. We start by drawing the 'big picture' of the scientific workflow development life cycle, before surveying and discussing current methods, technologies and practices for semantic domain modelling, automation in workflow development, and workflow assessment. Finally, we derive a roadmap of individual and community-based actions to work toward the vision of automated workflow development in the forthcoming years. A central outcome of the workshop is a general description of the workflow life cycle in six stages: 1) scientific question or hypothesis, 2) conceptual workflow, 3) abstract workflow, 4) concrete workflow, 5) production workflow, and 6) scientific results. The transitions between stages are facilitated by diverse tools and methods, usually incorporating domain knowledge in some form. Formal semantic domain modelling is hard and often a bottleneck for the application of semantic technologies. However, life science communities have made considerable progress here in recent years and are continuously improving, renewing interest in the application of semantic technologies for workflow exploration, composition and instantiation. Combined with systematic benchmarking with reference data and large-scale deployment of production-stage workflows, such technologies enable a more systematic process of workflow development than we know today. We believe that this can lead to more robust, reusable, and sustainable workflows in the future.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Lamprecht, Anna-Lena","Palmblad, Magnus","Ison, Jon","Schwämmle, Veit","Al Manir, Mohammad Sadnan","Altintas, Ilkay","Baker, Christopher J.O.","Ben Hadj Amor, Ammar","Capella-Gutierrez, Salvador","Charonyktakis, Paulos","Crusoe, Michael R.","Gil, Yolanda","Goble, Carole","Griffin, Timothy J.","Groth, Paul","Ienasescu, Hans","Jagtap, Pratik","Kalaš, Matúš","Kasalica, Vedran","Khanteymoori, Alireza","Kuhn, Tobias","Mei, Hailiang","Ménager, Hervé","Möller, Steffen","Richardson, Robin A.","Robert, Vincent","Soiland-Reyes, Stian","Stevens, Robert","Szaniszlo, Szoke","Verberne, Suzan","Verhoeven, Aswin","Wolstencroft, Katherine"],"cuid":["S02-094.59-034255"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ison, Jon","Lamprecht, Anna-Lena","Palmblad, Magnus","Schwämmle, Veit"],"country":["Canada","France","Germany","Greece","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Barcelona Supercomputing Center","Barcelona Supercomputing Center (BSC-CNS)","French Institute of Bioinformatics","Gnosis Data Analysis PC","IBIMA","IPSNP Computing Inc.","Institut Pasteur","Leiden University","Leiden University Medical Center","Netherlands eScience Center","Rostock University Medical Center","University of Amsterdam","University of Bergen","University of California at San Diego","University of California, San Diego","University of Freiburg","University of Manchester","University of Minnesota","University of Minnesota Minneapolis","University of New Brunswick","University of Southern California","University of Virginia","Utrecht University","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Vr