{"abstract":"The increasing excessive, automated or unaware use of smartphones calls for a better understanding and design of ‘mindful’ interactions with this device. In this 2-week study with 11 participants we focus on the influence of the operating system’s interface in inviting for ‘mindful’ or ‘mindless’ interactions. Patterns of smartphone use were studied with a standard interface for the first week, and a reconfigured interface for the second week - the reconfigured interface being designed for more intentional use. Based on the study results we formulate a set of 5 design research themes for mindful interaction, and illustrate them in a conceptual proposal.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kühn, Lena","Hermann, Charlotte","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381451"],"event":{"acronym":"SHI","title":"Scandinavian Conference on Health Informatics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human Computer Interaction","Interaction design","Mindful Interaction","Mobile technology","User Friendliness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design research themes for mindful interaction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84678766/ecp19161005.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381451","ids":["itu-0ca36e3f-44d6-4a63-8629-6e8510349c87"],"keyword":["Human Computer Interaction","Interaction Design","Mindful Interaction","Mobile Technology","User Friendliness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F56854384E3884B53B6009CA41A14F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ep.liu.se/ecp/161/005/ecp19161005.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84678766/ecp19161005.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"kühnpau","last":"Kühn","name":"Kühn, Lena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"hermannpau","last":"Hermann","name":"Hermann, Charlotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["16503740","9789179299576"],"isbn":["16503686"],"pages":"24-29","place":"Linköping","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 17th Scandinavian Conference on Health Informatics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0ca36e3f-44d6-4a63-8629-6e8510349c87"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Design Research Themes for Mindful Interaction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381451","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"There is growing evidence of the protective role of the Mediterranean diet (MD) on cancer. However, no prospective study has yet investigated its influence on lymphoma. We evaluated the association between adherence to the MD and risk of lymphoma and its subtypes in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC) study. The analysis included 476,160 participants, recruited from ten European countries between 1991 and 2001. Adherence to the MD was estimated through an adapted relative Mediterranean diet (arMED) score excluding alcohol. Cox proportional hazards regression models were used while adjusting for potential confounders. During an average follow-up of 13.9 years, 3,136 lymphomas (135 Hodgkin lymphoma (HL), 2,606 non-Hodgkin lymphoma and 395 lymphoma NOS) were identified. Overall, a 1-unit increase in the arMED score was associated with a 2% lower risk of lymphoma (95% CI: 0.97; 1.00, p-trend=0.03) while a statistically non-significant inverse association between a high versus low arMED score and risk of lymphoma was observed (HR: 0.91 (95% CI 0.80; 1.03), p-trend=0.12). Analyses by lymphoma subtype did not reveal any statistically significant associations. Albeit with small numbers of cases (N= 135), a suggestive inverse association was found for HL (HR 1-unit increase= 0.93 (95% CI: 0.86; 1.01), p-trend=0.07). However, the study may have lacked statistical power to detect small effect sizes for lymphoma subtype. Our findings suggest that an increasing arMED score was inversely related to the risk of overall lymphoma in EPIC, but not by subtypes. Further large prospective studies are warranted to confirm these findings. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":51,"contributors":["Solans, Marta","Benavente, Yolanda","Saez, Marc","Agudo, Antonio","Naudin, Sabine","Saberi Hosnijeh, Fatemeh","Noh, Hwayoung","Freisling, Heinz","Ferrari, Pietro","Besson, Caroline","Mahamat-Saleh, Yahya","Bout